$$
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & \frac{\hbar}{2}(-i) \\
i & 0
\end{bmatrix}
= 
\begin{bmatrix}
0 & -\frac{i\hbar}{2} \\
\frac{i\hbar}{2} & 0
\end{bmatrix}
$$

## Step 1: Compute the product of $\hbar/2$ and a 2x2 square matrix having elements in the first row as $(1, 0)$, and that in the second row as $(0, -1)$.

$$
\begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\hbar}{2} & 0 \\
0 & \frac{-\hbar}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\hbar}{2} & 0 \\
0 & -\frac{\hbar}{2}
\end{bmatrix}
$$

## Step 2: Write the elements of $P_z$ as a matrix.


$$
\begin{bmatrix}
\frac{\hbar}{2} & 0 \\
0 & -\frac{\hbar}{2}
